+// VR stereo: a perspective draw's projection for one eye. x and y come from the eye's frustum
+// (clip x = (2 x + (tanR + tanL) z) / (tanR - tanL), w = -z), z and w from the game's own
+// projection (its depth stays as it was), all applied to the view-space position moved into
+// the eye's space (view: 3x4 rows).
+//
+// Games draw a frame in pieces (Rogue Leader: a top and a bottom band, each with a viewport of
+// its height and an off-center frustum: x = p0 t - p1, y = p2 t - p3 for t = view tangent).
+// The eye's frustum stands for the whole frame, and each piece takes the same part of it the
+// game's took: scaled by frame / viewport size and moved by the game's own off-center term
+// (k, off below; 1 and 0 for a draw over the whole frame).
+struct StereoFit {
+  float kx = 1.f, ky = 1.f, offX = 0.f, offY = 0.f;
